#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Which of the eight adapters can serve a request - and how often the answer is none.

Every number in this skill's SKILL.md is printed by this script. It is deliberately
self-contained: it carries a dated SNAPSHOT of the three decisive flags per source, so it
runs on a bare install with no network and no vendor library, and it CROSS-CHECKS that
snapshot against `fin_skills.data.declare` when the generated package is importable, so
the copy cannot drift from the declarations it was taken from.

    python vendor_decision.py

The three flags, and why these three:

    includes_delisted   decides whether a result is an estimate or an UPPER BOUND. A
                        universe with no dead names in it cannot produce anything else.
    point_in_time       decides whether the source can answer "what was known at t?" - the
                        difference between a backtest and a demonstration that the past
                        was knowable in advance.
    redistribution      decides what you may do with what you fetched. It is a property of
                        the vendor's TERMS, not of the client library's SPDX licence, and
                        the two disagree for every free price source below.

Everything else - price, breadth, convenience, which Python client is nicest - is a
tiebreak between sources that have already survived those three.

No network, no vendor import, ASCII output, fixed data.
"""
